1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:06,624
今天继续介绍我用波函数坍缩算法，也就是 WFC，在建筑学方面的一些试验。
Today I continue with my experiments in architecture with the wave function collapse algorithm, WFC.

2
00:00:07,124 --> 00:00:10,062
也涉及到一点我个人学习图形技术的故事。
It is also a little of my own story of learning graphics programming.

3
00:00:10,562 --> 00:00:17,800
我必须补充，是我一位朋友——网名 P小二 的 AI 行业专家，也是著名创业者和 UP 主
I should add that it was a friend of mine, known online as P小二, an AI expert, well-known founder and video creator,

4
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:21,419
在我刚刚上手自学的时候，提示我关注这一算法。
who pointed me to this algorithm when I had just begun teaching myself.

5
00:00:23,919 --> 00:00:29,033
WFC 算法存在内在局限，不适合解决层次非常丰富的问题。
WFC has inherent limits: it does not suit problems with many layers of hierarchy.

6
00:00:29,533 --> 00:00:33,907
但是它适合构建建筑学构造层次的一些基本逻辑。
But it does suit building some of the basic logic at the tectonic level of architecture.

7
00:00:34,407 --> 00:00:38,129
我们一旦学会了它，自然要榨取其中的价值。
Once we have learned it, we naturally want to squeeze the value out of it

8
00:00:38,129 --> 00:00:42,224
并且从我们本身背景行业出发，吸取其中的启发。
and, starting from our own profession, draw inspiration from it.

9
00:00:42,724 --> 00:00:49,711
2022 年，在户型生成算法仅仅大致跑通的情况下，我寻找到了下一个实验对象——古建筑。
In 2022, with my floor plan generator only roughly working, I found the next subject to experiment on: historical architecture.

10
00:00:50,211 --> 00:00:55,142
古建筑的本质也是层次丰富的，不过它的构造，经常是套路化的。
Historical architecture is also rich in hierarchy by nature, but its construction often follows set routines.

11
00:00:55,642 --> 00:00:59,298
这些套路，有时候在表面上定义它自身的形式。
Those routines sometimes define its very form, on the surface.

12
00:01:01,998 --> 00:01:07,797
偏巧我当时从 Bruno Simon 的网课上接触了一些三维网页技术，使我有动力开工进行这个实验。
As it happened, I had just picked up some 3D web technology from Bruno Simon's online course, which gave me the drive to start this experiment.

13
00:01:08,297 --> 00:01:12,900
算法知识来自于 Oskar Stålberg 和 Daniel Shiffman 教授的讲座。
The knowledge of the algorithm came from the talks of Oskar Stålberg and Professor Daniel Shiffman.

14
00:01:13,400 --> 00:01:19,330
特别是 Shiffman 教授的讲座，给出了简明、而且我相对擅长的 JavaScript 代码。
Professor Shiffman's lecture in particular gave concise code in JavaScript, a language I am fairly at home in.

15
00:01:19,830 --> 00:01:22,247
这些就是这个项目的起点。
These are where this project started.

16
00:01:24,647 --> 00:01:28,424
WFC 最为人知的用途，是生成游戏关卡。
WFC is best known for generating game levels.

17
00:01:28,924 --> 00:01:33,148
从建筑师的角度，我们看重的，是它作为构造的语法。
From an architect's point of view, what we value is its use as a tectonic grammar.

18
00:01:33,648 --> 00:01:38,598
适合自下而上构造化的产生秩序，在构件与构件的交接处。
It suits producing order from the bottom up, tectonically, where one component meets another.

19
00:01:39,098 --> 00:01:43,741
屋脊怎样相接，檐口怎样转角，天沟能不能出现。
How ridges meet, how eaves turn a corner, whether a gutter may appear.

20
00:01:44,241 --> 00:01:50,449
这些交接的规矩，正是传统木构建筑最精炼的知识和一些自然的法则。
These rules of joining are the most distilled knowledge of traditional timber architecture, and some laws of nature.

21
00:01:50,949 --> 00:01:56,687
在它形成一个构造基础之上，要施加什么更宏观的秩序，是另外一个层次的问题。
What larger order to impose on top of this tectonic base is a question on another level.

22
00:01:57,187 --> 00:02:02,047
我们这个实验是暂时排除更上层问题的。那是下一个实验的问题。
This experiment sets those higher questions aside for now. They belong to the next experiment.

23
00:02:04,547 --> 00:02:10,839
积木的种类是非常有限的，阴角、阳角、边缘、中腹，几种不同的形式而已。
The kinds of block are very few: inside corners, outside corners, edges and middles, only a handful of forms.

24
00:02:11,339 --> 00:02:16,523
两个块相邻，只要相对的两条边的剖面吻合，就能拼在一起。
Two neighbouring blocks fit together as long as the sections of their facing edges agree.

25
00:02:17,023 --> 00:02:23,954
代码实际上简单得惊人，只是把每块积木的边缘编码，每个边缘用 3 个字符表示。
The code is surprisingly simple: it just encodes the edges of every block, three characters to an edge.

26
00:02:24,454 --> 00:02:29,357
这些字符是对这些边缘形状的抽象，主要表示高度轮廓。
The characters abstract the shape of an edge, mainly its profile of heights.

27
00:02:29,857 --> 00:02:32,808
0 是地面，-1 是水底；
Zero is the ground and minus one the water bottom;

28
00:02:32,808 --> 00:02:42,795
1 是檐口，2 是进深较浅部分的矮脊，3 是进深较大的房屋的高的屋脊，4，是二层的檐口。
one is the eave, two the low ridge of the shallower part, three the high ridge of the deeper building, and four the eave of the upper storey.

29
00:02:43,295 --> 00:02:49,479
用一些条件语句来判断两块积木的边能否拼合。拼合不了的地方会给出报警。
A few conditional statements decide whether two edges can join. Where they cannot, a warning is shown.

30
00:02:49,979 --> 00:02:52,824
有个别的情况需要人为写一些代码来排除。
A few cases have to be ruled out with code written by hand.

31
00:02:53,324 --> 00:02:57,223
比如，两片下坡的屋面不能对撞，形成积水的天沟；
For example, two roofs sloping down may not meet in a gutter that holds water,

32
00:02:57,223 --> 00:02:59,765
两个凹角不能相对，形成一个坑。
and two valley corners may not face each other and form a pit.

33
00:03:02,465 --> 00:03:09,910
这些规则，最早是在笔记本上一格一格画出来的。每个块编号，每条边写上高度。
These rules were first drawn cell by cell in a notebook. Every block numbered, every edge labelled with its heights.

34
00:03:10,410 --> 00:03:14,612
后来整理成 32 个块，之后我又简化到 24 个块。
Later they were sorted into 32 blocks, which I then reduced to 24.

35
00:03:15,112 --> 00:03:19,254
其中有一些是和地面、水面、小桥之类景观元素有关的。
Some of them are landscape elements: ground, water, a small bridge.

36
00:03:21,954 --> 00:03:24,403
建模在 Blender 里进行。
The modelling is done in Blender.

37
00:03:24,403 --> 00:03:28,996
用的仍然是我 2023 年手动建的。当时花了大概一整个周末。
The models are still the ones I built by hand in 2023, which took about a whole weekend.

38
00:03:29,496 --> 00:03:33,081
即便现在，这种模型，也很难交给 AI 去建。
Even now such models are hard to hand over to AI,

39
00:03:33,081 --> 00:03:37,645
因为 AI 暂时对这种多维度的目标，把握能力还比较有限。
whose grasp of a target with this many dimensions is still limited.

40
00:03:38,145 --> 00:03:40,445
不知道再过一年会是什么情况。
Who knows how that will look in another year.

41
00:03:43,345 --> 00:03:47,293
生成的时候，每一格先处在所有可能的叠加之中。
When generating, every cell starts in a superposition of all possibilities.

42
00:03:47,793 --> 00:03:53,531
可能性最少的那一格先坍缩，它的选择，又排除了邻居的一部分可能。
The cell with the fewest possibilities collapses first, and its choice rules out some of its neighbours' options.

43
00:03:54,031 --> 00:03:59,252
一格接一格，建筑、檐廊、池塘，从局部的规则里长出来。
Cell by cell, buildings, verandas and ponds grow out of local rules.

44
00:03:59,752 --> 00:04:04,654
这种生成的结果是相当散漫的。因为这里面没有给出任何的评价方式。
The results generated this way are rather loose, because nothing in here evaluates them.

45
00:04:05,154 --> 00:04:08,995
散漫的结果，看起来就不像相对整齐的宋明官式古建，
Loose as they are, they look less like the fairly regular official architecture of the Song and Ming dynasties,

46
00:04:08,995 --> 00:04:14,917
而更像日本室町时代的武家住宅格式，也称书院造（Shoin-zukuri）。
and more like the warrior residences of Japan's Muromachi period, the style called shoin-zukuri.

47
00:04:18,417 --> 00:04:24,169
由于 vibe coding 的成熟，我最近增加了一些功能，可以手动在里面增减建筑的体量。
Now that vibe coding has matured, I recently added features to add and remove building volumes by hand.

48
00:04:24,669 --> 00:04:26,934
这种玩法和 Townscaper 大体一致。
This way of playing is much the same as Townscaper.

49
00:04:30,234 --> 00:04:33,566
这个系统，不只能在横平竖直的网格里进行，
The system does not only work on a straight, square grid;

50
00:04:33,566 --> 00:04:37,065
也能放进任何，或固定或自由的四边形网格里。
it can go into any grid of quads, fixed or free.

51
00:04:37,565 --> 00:04:41,063
比如 Stålberg 在他的游戏设计中使用的网格。
For example the grid Stålberg uses in his game design.

52
00:04:41,563 --> 00:04:46,178
在一个轻微扭曲的网格里，生成结果显示出貌似的有机性。
On a gently bent grid, the results show a seemingly organic quality.

53
00:04:46,678 --> 00:04:50,986
而在扭动剧烈的网格里，则显得相当现代和高技派。
On a strongly twisted grid, they look quite modern, even high-tech.

54
00:04:51,486 --> 00:04:53,658
我从中甚至得到了一些启发，
I even took something from this:

55
00:04:53,658 --> 00:04:58,671
其实古建，如果放弃标准化的尺寸，其实造型上可以相当令人意外。
historical architecture, once it gives up standardized dimensions, can be quite surprising in form.

56
00:05:02,171 --> 00:05:04,773
换一套积木，就可以产生另一套风格。
Swap in another set of blocks, and you get another style.

57
00:05:05,273 --> 00:05:09,115
多套积木的拼合，就可以形成类型学混合。
Join several sets of blocks, and you get a mixture of typologies.

58
00:05:09,615 --> 00:05:14,629
用另一套力学来支配这种混合的方式，就会产生更高层级的秩序。
Let another set of forces govern how they mix, and an order of a higher level appears.

59
00:05:15,129 --> 00:05:17,017
这就是这套方法的探索方向。
That is the direction this method is exploring.
